  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training of trainers on conflict analysis and sensitivity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM operates in some of the world&apos;s most fragile and conflict-affected contexts, where interventions are never conflict-neutral and can carry both operational risks and unintended impacts on conflict dynamics. Ensuring that programmes avoid harm and, where possible, contribute to conditions for peace and stability is therefore essential. Conflict sensitivity is a cross-cutting institutional principle underpinning IOM&apos;s work across departments and functions, and closely aligned with its commitments under the Humanitarian-Development-Peace Nexus. Building on previous institutional investments, this project&apos;s overall objective is to strengthen IOM internal capacity to apply conflict sensitivity across IOM programmes, operations, and institutional processes. Its intended outcome is the enhanced ability of regional office personnel to support the application of conflict sensitivity. The principle project output is a three-day training of trainers on conflict analysis and sensitivity, through which IOM will equip participants with the technical knowledge and facilitation skills to effectively accompany country offices in the application of conflict sensitivity within their respective regions.</narrative>
  </description>
